From 17a87436c7fb77a222917a4f6978597b1b46ef4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:56:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] held-default stall: a stale or draining machine is
 not a default-card taker

PR #2264 review 5892044674 (nit 1, t_01a1d5278ec3d702): `others_take_default` counted any active,
non-explicit-pickup machine that passed `kanban_worker_node.eligible` as able to copy a held machine's
default-placement card. It never checked `last_seen` freshness or `metrics.drain_active`, which
`alarm_placement` checks through `_ready_now`. A stale or draining non-explicit machine claims nothing, yet it
suppressed the held-default stall alarm for a card no one could take (fail-open). No live registry machine has
non-explicit pickup today, so nothing was affected yet.

Fix: factor `kanban_pickup_stall._live` (not draining, last_seen within FRESH_SECONDS) out of `_ready_now`, and
make `others_take_default` require it, with `now_ms` passed from `stranded` (keyword-only, so no caller can skip
it). The free-slot part of `_ready_now` is deliberately not applied: a full machine still copies the card and runs
it when a slot frees, so it is a taker.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pickup_stall_held.py):
- new test_a_stale_or_draining_default_taker_does_not_silence_the_alarm[stale|draining]: held worker-6 with its
  own ready default card, worker-1 on `pickup: all` but stale (last_seen FRESH_SECONDS+60 s before the sweep) or
  drain_active -> the alarm files. RED on main cd40d134de (both fail), GREEN after.
- test_t3_no_alarm_when_another_machine_can_claim_the_card now stamps last_seen at the simulated sweep time
  (fresh, not draining) -> still no alarm.
- All 9 suites importing kanban_pickup_stall*: 228 passed; scripts/check --base origin/main: 19 checks ok.
